menu "TouchDeck perf tools (test builds only)"

    config TD_PERF_TOOLS
        bool "Build the perf measurement commands"
        default n
        select FREERTOS_GENERATE_RUN_TIME_STATS
        select FREERTOS_VTASKLIST_INCLUDE_COREID
        help
            Adds `perf info`, `perf window`, `perf tap`, `perf mem`, `perf cpu`, `perf fb`, `perf invalidate`,
            `perf stall`, `perf memtest`, `perf membw` and `perf temp` to the console and gives `perf fps` panel,
            render, copy and CPU figures. It wraps two esp_lcd calls at link time, turns on FreeRTOS run-time stats
            and never formats a storage volume that will not mount, so it is for test builds only. Build it from
            firmware/perf/tools.defaults into a build directory of its own, never into the committed sdkconfig. Off,
            the firmware compiles to the same code as without it.

    config TD_PERF_VARIANT
        string "Build name that perf info reports"
        depends on TD_PERF_TOOLS
        default "baseline"
        help
            Names the build under test, so a bench can prove which build is flashed. A defaults file listed after
            firmware/perf/tools.defaults sets it.

endmenu

menu "TouchDeck display"

    config TD_PAY_COPY_DEBT
        bool "Bring lagging frame buffers up to date while LVGL is idle"
        default y
        help
            In the adapter's triple-partial mode a refresh that redraws at least a quarter of the screen, such as a
            page slide's frame, leaves the two other frame buffers behind, and each of the next two refreshes copies
            that area into one of them, about 60 ms for the whole screen. With this on, 120 ms after the last such
            refresh, and only while no area waits to be drawn, no animation runs and no pointer is pressed, LVGL
            redraws one unchanged pixel twice, so those copies happen before the next touch and not in its refresh.
            The pixels on the panel stay the same. Off, the next refreshes pay the copies, so the first tap after a
            page slide waits for them.

endmenu
